<title>MOLDOVA: MOLDOVAN SPECIALISED INSURANCE BOND YIELD FALLS.</title>
<headline>MOLDOVAN SPECIALISED INSURANCE BOND YIELD FALLS.</headline>
<dateline>CHISINAU 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on Moldovan 365-day</p>
<p>specialised insurance bonds fell at auction on Tuesday to 36.90</p>
<p>percent annually from 38.55 percent at their first auction a</p>
<p>week ago, a National Bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Full details of the 365-day insurance bonds auction:</p>
<p>				    Dec 10		 Dec 3</p>
<p>    Issue volume		4.00 mln lei	 2.00 mln lei</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1,000 lei	    1,000 lei</p>
<p>    Nominal demand	    4.60 mln	     5.66 mln</p>
<p>    Volume sold		 4.00 mln	     2.00 mln</p>
<p>    Yield			 36.90 pct	    38.55 pct</p>
<p>    Price			 84.0 pct	     83.0 pct</p>
<p>    Range of bids	     84.0-86.0 pct	83.0-90.0 pct</p>
<p>    Maturity		    Dec 12, 1997	 Dec 5, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE: The yield includes a fixed annual income of 15</p>
<p>percent guaranteed by the Finance Ministry.</p>
</text>
